[HEADING=1][DD] Bump[/HEADING]

[B][DD] Bump[/B] is a developer CLI tool for XenForo 2.3 that automates semantic version bumping for add-ons according to official XenForo standards.

[HEADING=2]Features[/HEADING]
[LIST]
[*][B]Semantic Versioning[/B]: Calculates and increments Major, Minor, Patch, Alpha, Beta, RC, and Stable version IDs.
[*][B]Synchronized Updates[/B]: Simultaneously updates [ICODE]addon.json[/ICODE] and the [ICODE]xf_addon[/ICODE] database table in a single step.
[*][B]Interactive Console[/B]: Prompts for bump type interactively when executed without parameters.
[*][B]Safety Controls[/B]: Includes [ICODE]--dry-run[/ICODE] to preview changes and [ICODE]--force[/ICODE] to bypass validation if needed.
[/LIST]

[HEADING=2]Requirements[/HEADING]
[LIST]
[*]XenForo 2.3.0+, PHP 8.2.0+
[/LIST]

[HEADING=2]Usage[/HEADING]
Execute the [ICODE]dd:bump[/ICODE] command in your XenForo root directory:

[CODE=bash]php cmd.php dd:bump Vendor/Addon [type] [state][/CODE]

[HEADING=3]Parameters & Options[/HEADING]
[LIST]
[*][B]Vendor/Addon[/B]: The ID of the add-on to bump (e.g. [ICODE]cv6/DiceRoller[/ICODE]).
[*][B]type[/B] [I](optional)[/I]: Bump type ([ICODE]major[/ICODE], [ICODE]minor[/ICODE], [ICODE]patch[/ICODE], [ICODE]alpha[/ICODE], [ICODE]beta[/ICODE], [ICODE]rc[/ICODE], [ICODE]stable[/ICODE]).
[*][B]state[/B] [I](optional)[/I]: Specific state override if setting release candidate or stability levels.
[*][B]--dry-run[/B]: Preview version changes without modifying files or database.
[*][B]--force[/B] ([ICODE]-f[/ICODE]): Skip validation of version ID.
[/LIST]

[HEADING=3]Examples[/HEADING]
[LIST]
[*][B]Patch bump[/B] (e.g. 1.0.0 -> 1.0.1):
[CODE=bash]php cmd.php dd:bump Vendor/Addon patch[/CODE]
[*][B]Minor bump[/B] (e.g. 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0):
[CODE=bash]php cmd.php dd:bump Vendor/Addon minor[/CODE]
[*][B]Change stability to stable[/B]:
[CODE=bash]php cmd.php dd:bump Vendor/Addon stable[/CODE]
[*][B]Interactive prompt[/B]:
[CODE=bash]php cmd.php dd:bump Vendor/Addon[/CODE]
[/LIST]
